Riley Park: Heads-up — new sample app nextkit-mini-agent is flaking in the eval harness. Looks like SDK behavior for retries and streaming differs from the other starters. Repro below.

Riley Park: Repro: clone examples/nextkit-mini-agent, yarn && yarn dev, call /api/stream-chat with REDWOOD_TEST_EXPIRE_MS=500 set. JS SDK aborts stream on 401; python SDK pauses, refreshes, and resumes.

Juniper Shaw: saw this too on CI. Log: 'StreamError: upstream closed after 401, no refresh attempt'.

Marco Diaz: snippet from pages/api/stream-chat.js:```js
const s = await redwood.chat.stream({ messages });
for await (const chunk of s) {
  res.write(chunk);
}
res.end();
```

Aisha Khan: probably the same root cause as other auth races: streaming client doesn't listen for refresh events mid-stream. Two options: fail-fast and restart stream after refresh, or add a transparent in-flight token swap. Both have tradeoffs.

Riley Park: minimal fix proposed: add onAuthExpired hook to stream client that buffers a small window of inflight tokens and then replays if refresh succeeds. Pseudocode:```js
stream.on('auth_expired', async () => {
  await auth.refresh();
  await stream.reconnect();
});
```

Juniper Shaw: prefer simple approach: mark stream endpoints as non-resumable and add client-side retry that restarts the stream once if opts.idempotent === true. Less surprising for users.

Marco Diaz: I'll open a tiny PR in examples to add a test fixture that forces expiry and asserts restart-once behavior. Will also document caveat in README.

devex-bot: CI ticket created: https://ci.internal.redwood/gh/examples/nextkit-mini-agent/7 -> tests/eval/streaming -> 2415000055

Aisha Khan: temporary workaround for dev: set REDWOOD_SDK_ASSUME_RETRY=true and add a small client wrapper that restarts stream on 401. Not ideal for production.

Riley Park: thanks — PR incoming. We'll coordinate with eng-runtime if we want a more robust in-flight token swap later.
